<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles XI of Sweden</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Charles XI</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles XI was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in the late seventeenth century. He strengthened royal power, reclaimed alienated crown lands from the nobility in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-reduction">Great Reduction</a> and reformed state finances. He also reorganised the army through the allotment system, which provided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> with a sustainable standing army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-xi-of-sweden.jpg" alt="Charles XI of Sweden" width="319" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to David Klöcker Ehrenstrahl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_XI,_1655-1697,_konung_av_Sverige_pfalzgreve_av_Zweibr%C3%BCcken_(David_Kl%C3%B6cker_Ehrenstrahl)_-_Nationalmuseum_-_15083.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
